\par\par \b \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank Issue of Debt\b0\par\par\uc2 5,173 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2019\par 08:00\par \uc2 Regulatory News Service\par \uc2 RNS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2019 \par \par \uc2 TIDM42BI\par \par \uc2 RNS Number : 5185S\par \par \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank\par \par \uc2 11 March 2019\par \par \uc2 PRICING SUPPLEMENT\par \par \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank\par \par \uc2 Global Debt Program\par \par \uc2 Series No.: 553\par \par \uc2 Tranche No.: 12\par \par \uc2 IDR 674,000,000,000 7.875 percent Notes due March 14, 2023 (the "Notes") as from March 11, 2019 to be consolidated and form a single series with the Bank's\par \par \uc2 IDR 950,000,000,000 7.875 percent Notes due March 14, 2023, issued on March 14, 2016 (the "Series 553 Tranche 1 Notes"), the Bank's IDR 327,250,000,000 7.875 percent Notes due March 14, 2023, issued on November 18, 2016 (the "Series 553 Tranche 2 Notes"), the Bank's IDR 334,000,000,000 7.875 percent Notes due March 14, 2023, issued on May 24, 2017 (the "Series 553 Tranche 3 Notes"), the Bank's\par \par \uc2 IDR 1,332,000,000,000 7.875 percent Notes due March 14, 2023, issued on July 27, 2017 (the "Series 553 Tranche 4 Notes"), the Bank's IDR 250,000,000,000 7.875 percent Notes due March 14, 2023, issued on September 19, 2017 (the "Series 553 Tranche 5 Notes"), the Bank's IDR 1,645,000,000,000 7.875 percent Notes due March 14, 2023, issued on November 14, 2017 (the "Series 553 Tranche 6 Notes"), the Bank's IDR 800,000,000,000 7.875 percent Notes due March 14, 2023, issued on December 7, 2017 (the "Series 553 Tranche 7 Notes"), the Bank's IDR 250,000,000,000 7.875 percent Notes due March 14, 2023, issued on December 18, 2017 (the "Series 553 Tranche 8 Notes"), the Bank's IDR 670,800,000,000 7.875 percent Notes due March 14, 2023, issued on January 24, 2018 (the "Series 553 Tranche 9 Notes"), the Bank's IDR 360,000,000,000 7.875 percent Notes due March 14, 2023, issued on July 26, 2018 (the "Series 553 Tranche 10 Notes") and the Bank's IDR 850,000,000,000 7.875 percent Notes due March 14, 2023, issued on February 20, 2019 (the "Series 553 Tranche 11 Notes")\par \par \uc2 payable in United States Dollars\par \par \uc2 Issue Price: 101.459107 percent plus 362 days' accrued interest\par \par \uc2 Application has been made for the Notes to be admitted to the Official List of the United Kingdom Listing Authority and to trading on the \uc2 London Stock Exchange plc\uc2 's Regulated Market\par \par \uc2 J.P. Morgan\par \par \uc2 The date of this Pricing Supplement is as of March 6, 2019\par \par \uc2 Terms used herein shall be deemed to be defined as such for the purposes of the Terms and Conditions (the "Conditions") set forth in the Prospectus dated January 8, 2001 (the "Prospectus") (which for the avoidance of doubt does not constitute a prospectus for the purposes of Part VI of the United Kingdom Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 or a base prospectus for the purposes of Directive 2003/71/EC of the \uc2 European Parliament\uc2  and of the Council). This Pricing Supplement must be read in conjunction with the Prospectus. This document is issued to give details of an issue by the \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank\uc2  (the "Bank") under its Global Debt Program and to provide information supplemental to the Prospectus. Complete information in respect of the Bank and this offer of the Notes is only available on the basis of the combination of this Pricing Supplement and the Prospectus.\par \par \uc2 MiFID II product governance / Retail investors, professional investors and ECPs target market - See "General Information-Additional Information Regarding the Notes-Matters relating to MiFID II" below.\par \par \uc2 Terms and Conditions\par \par \uc2 The following items under this heading "Terms and Conditions" are the particular terms which relate to the issue the subject of this Pricing Supplement. These are the only terms which form part of the form of Notes for such issue. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  1.    Series No.:                      553 \par         Tranche No.:                     12 \par  2.    Aggregate Principal Amount:      IDR 674,000,000,000 \par                                          As from the Issue Date, the Notes \par                                          will be consolidated and form \par                                          a single series with the Series \par                                          553 Tranche 1 Notes, the Series \par                                          553 Tranche 2 Notes, the Series \par                                          553 Tranche 3 Notes, the Series \par                                          553 Tranche 4 Notes, the Series \par                                          553 Tranche 5 Notes, the Series \par                                          553 Tranche 6 Notes, the Series \par                                          553 Tranche 7 Notes, the Series \par                                          553 Tranche 8 Notes, the Series \par                                          553 Tranche 9 Notes, the Series \par                                          553 Tranche 10 Notes and the Series \par                                          553 Tranche 11 Notes. \par  3.    Issue Price:                        IDR 736,475,627,940.00 which amount \par                                            represents the sum of (a) 101.459107 \par                                             percent of the Aggregate Principal \par                                                Amount plus (b) the amount of \par                                             IDR 52,641,246,760.00 representing \par                                           362 days' accrued interest, inclusive. \par                                               The Issue Price will be payable \par                                          in USD in the amount of USD 52,474,216.45 \par                                              at the agreed rate of 14,035 IDR \par                                                        per one USD. \par  4.    Issue Date:                      March 11, 2019 \par  5.    Form of Notes \par         (Condition 1(a)):                Registered only, as further provided \par                                          in paragraph 9(c) of "Other Relevant \par                                          Terms" below. \par  6.    Authorized Denomination(s) \par          (Condition 1(b)):               IDR 10,000,000 and integral multiples \par                                          thereof \par  7.    Specified \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par         (Condition 1(d)):                The lawful \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the Republic \par                                          of Indonesia ("Indonesian Rupiah" \par                                          or "IDR"), provided that all payments \par                                          in respect of the Notes will be \par                                          made in United States Dollars \par                                          ("U.S.$" or "USD") \par  8.    Specified Principal Payment \par         \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par         (Conditions 1(d) and 7(h)):      USD \par  9.    Specified Interest Payment \par         \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                          USD \par         (Conditions 1(d) and 7(h)): \par  10.   Maturity Date \par         (Condition 6(a); Fixed            March 14, 2023 \par         Interest Rate): \par  11.   Interest Basis \par         (Condition 5):                   Fixed Interest Rate (Condition \par                                          5(I)) \par  12.   Interest Commencement Date \par         (Condition 5(III)):               March 14, 2018 \par  13.   Fixed Interest Rate (Condition   Condition 5(I) as amended and \par         5(I)):                           supplemented below, shall apply \par                                          to the Notes. The bases of the \par                                          Calculation of the Interest Amount, \par                                          Interest Payment Dates and default \par                                          interest are as set out below. \par  \par          (a) Interest Rate:              7.875 percent per annum \par        (b) Business Day Convention:     Following Business Day Convention \par        (c) Fixed Rate Interest \par         Payment Date(s):                  Annually on each March 14, commencing \par                                           on March 14, 2019 and ending on, \par                                           and including, the Maturity Date. \par                                           Each Interest Payment Date is \par                                           subject to adjustment in accordance \par                                           with the Following Business Day \par                                           Convention with no adjustment \par                                           to the amount of interest otherwise \par                                           calculated. \par        (d) Interest Period:             Each period from and including \par                                          each Interest Payment Date to \par                                          but excluding the next following \par                                          Interest Payment Date, provided \par                                          that the initial Interest Period \par                                          will commence on and include the \par                                          Interest Commencement Date, and \par                                          the final Interest Period will \par                                          end on but exclude the Maturity \par                                          Date. \par                                          For the purposes of the calculation \par                                          of the Interest Amount payable \par                                          for any Interest Period, there \par                                          shall be no adjustment pursuant \par                                          to the Business Day Convention \par                                          specified above. \par        (e) Fixed Rate Day Count \par         Fraction(s):                     Actual/Actual \f28 \uc2 \f2 ICMA\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par        (f) Calculation of Interest      As soon as practicable and in \par         Amount:                          accordance with the procedure \par                                          specified herein, the Calculation \par                                          Agent will determine the IDR Rate \par                                          (as defined below) and calculate \par                                          the amount of interest payable \par                                          (the "Interest Amount") with respect \par                                          to each minimum Authorized Denomination \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Inter-American Development Bank Issue of Debt -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                          for the relevant Interest Period. \par                                          The Interest Amount with respect \par                                          to any Interest Period shall be \par                                          a USD amount calculated on the \par                                          relevant Rate Fixing Date (as \par                                          defined below) as follows: \par                                          7.875% times the minimum Authorized \par                                          Denomination \par  \par                                          times \par  \par                                          the Fixed Rate Day Count Fraction \par  \par                                          divided by \par  \par                                          the IDR Rate \par  \par                                          (and rounding, if necessary, the \par                                          entire resulting figure to the \par                                          nearest two decimal places, with \par                                          USD 0.005 being rounded upwards). \par  \par                                          The "IDR Rate" means the rate \par                                          determined by the Calculation \par                                          Agent that is equal to the USD/IDR \par                                          weighted average spot rate in \par                                          the interbank market, based on \par                                          traded USD/IDR spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par                                          transactions during a specified \par                                          time period which are captured \par                                          on a real time basis, expressed \par                                          as the amount of IDR per one USD, \par                                          for settlement in two Fixing Business \par                                          Days, as published by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par                                          as the "Jakarta Interbank Spot \par                                          Dollar Rate USD - IDR", which \par                                          appears on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's website \par                                          (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bi.go.id"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bi.go.id}}}\uc2 \f2 ), or as published \par                                          on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thomson Reuters\f28 \uc2 \f2  Screen JISDOR \par                                          Page (or any replacement page \par                                          or replacement service as may \par                                          be implemented for the purposes \par                                          of displaying the USD/IDR weighted \par                                          average spot rate), or as otherwise \par                                          made available by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par                                          (or its successor as administrator), \par                                          at approximately 10:00 a.m., Jakarta \par                                          time, on the Rate Fixing Date. \par                                          Fallback Provisions apply as set \par                                          out below. \par                                         The "Rate Fixing Date" means the \par                                          date that is five (5) Fixing Business \par                                          Days prior to the applicable Fixed \par                                          Rate Interest Payment Date or \par                                          Maturity Date, as the case may \par                                          be. The Rate Fixing Date shall \par                                          be subject to adjustment as follows: \par                                          if the scheduled date of the Rate \par                                          Fixing Date is not a Relevant \par                                          Business Day, then the Rate Fixing \par                                          Date will be the first preceding \par                                          day that is a Relevant Business \par                                          Day. \par                                          "Fixing Business Day" means a \par                                          day (other than a Saturday or \par                                          a Sunday) on which banks and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign \par                                          exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets are open for \par                                          business in Jakarta. \par                                         "Fallback Provisions": Should \par                                          no USD/IDR weighted average spot \par                                          rate appear on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \par                                          website (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bi.go.id"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bi.go.id}}}\uc2 \f2 ) as the \par                                          "Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar \par                                          Rate USD - IDR", or on Thomson \par                                          Reuters Screen JISDOR Page (or \par                                          on such replacement page or replacement \par                                          service as described above), or \par                                          be otherwise made available by \par                                          \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  (or its successor \par                                          as administrator), on the Rate \par                                          Fixing Date, then the IDR Rate \par                                          for such Rate Fixing Date shall \par                                          be determined by the Calculation \par                                          Agent by requesting quotations \par                                          for the mid USD/IDR spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign \par                                          exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate from five banks \par                                          active in the USD/IDR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par                                          and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets as \par                                          selected by the Calculation Agent \par                                          (such banks, the "Reference Banks") \par                                          either (i) at or about 10:00 a.m. \par                                          Jakarta time on the first day \par                                          (other than a Saturday or a Sunday) \par                                          following the Rate Fixing Date, \par                                          if such day is a Relevant Business \par                                          Day or (ii) at or about 10:00 \par                                          a.m. Jakarta time on the Rate \par                                          Fixing Date, if the first day \par                                          (other than a Saturday or a Sunday) \par                                          following the Rate Fixing Date \par                                          is not a Relevant Business Day. \par                                         If five or four quotations are \par                                          provided by Reference Banks as \par                                          requested, the IDR Rate shall \par                                          be the arithmetic mean (rounded \par                                          to the nearest whole IDR, with \par                                          IDR 0.5 being rounded upwards) \par                                          of the remaining three or two \par                                          such 