y replacement page or replacement \par                                                              service as may be implemented for \par                                                              the purposes of displaying the USD/IDR \par                                                              weighted average spot rate), or as \par                                                              otherwise made available by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par                                                              (or its successor as administrator), \par                                                              at approximately 10:00 a.m., Jakarta \par                                                              time, on the Rate Fixing Date. Fallback \par                                                              Provisions apply as set out below. \par                                                             The "Rate Fixing Date" means the date \par                                                              that is five (5) Fixing Business Days \par                                                              prior to the applicable Fixed Rate \par                                                              Interest Payment Date or Maturity \par                                                              Date, as the case may be. The Rate \par                                                              Fixing Date shall be subject to adjustment \par                                                              as follows: if the scheduled date \par                                                              of the Rate Fixing Date is not a Relevant \par                                                              Business Day, then the Rate Fixing \par                                                              Date will be the first preceding day \par                                                              that is a Relevant Business Day. \par                                                              "Fixing Business Day" means a day \par                                                              (other than a Saturday or a Sunday) \par                                                              on which banks and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par                                                              markets are open for business in Jakarta. \par                                                             "Fallback Provisions": Should no USD/IDR \par                                                              weighted average spot rate appear \par                                                              on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's website (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bi.go.id"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bi.go.id}}}\uc2 \f2 ) \par                                                              as the "Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar \par                                                              Rate USD - IDR", or on Thomson Reuters \par                                                              Screen JISDOR Page (or on such replacement \par                                                              page or replacement service as described \par                                                              above), or be otherwise made available \par                                                              by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  (or its successor \par                                                              as administrator), on the Rate Fixing \par                                                              Date, then the IDR Rate for such Rate \par                                                              Fixing Date shall be determined by \par                                                              the Calculation Agent by requesting \par     