\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asian units climb as dollar slips on Fed comments; rupiah leads gains\b0\par\par\uc2 640 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2019\par 06:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Aby Jose Koilparambil\par     Jan 7 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthened\par across the board on Monday as the dollar retreated following\par comments by Federal Reserve Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jerome Powell\f28 \uc2 \f2  that boosted\par risk appetites.\par     Powell on Friday said the Fed is not on a preset path of\par interest rate hikes and suggested that it could pause its policy\par tightening as it did in 2016.\par     His pledge of sensitivity to downside risks the market was\par pricing in meant the greenback gave up all the gains logged\par after December data released earlier on Friday showed U.S.\par employers hired the most workers in 10 months while boosting\par wages.\par     "The improvement in risk appetite, together with Powell's\par latest comments, may continue to see the USD stall... In the\par interim, (we) expect investors to ride the cyclicals and EM \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par higher on the back of improved appetite," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 OCBC Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a\par note.\par     Risk appetites were also whetted by China's aggressive\par monetary easing announced on Friday and this week's meeting of\par U.S. and Chinese officials for the first face-to-face talks\par since both countries in December agreed to a 90-day truce in a\par their trade war.\par     The Indonesian rupiah led Monday's gains, rising as\par much as 1.9 percent to 13,990 to the dollar, its strongest level\par in more than six months.\par     The Korean won rose as much as 0.8 percent to\par 1,115.50 against the dollar, while the Indian rupee\par gained up to 0.7 percent, touching its strongest point since\par Aug. 10.\par     The Malaysian ringgit firmed as much as 0.6 percent\par to 4.108 against the dollar, its best since August.\par     The Thai baht and Chinese yuan both\par appreciated as much as 0.4 percent. The Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  scaled its\par best level in seven months.\par     \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par     The appreciation in rupiah was also aided by a statement\par that the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the domestic\par non-deliverable forward (NDF) market to provide liquidity.\par     Nanang Hendarsah, head of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary\par management, said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will be conducted through\par brokers, separate from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's daily auction to boost\par the volume of the domestic NDF transactions and deepen the\par market for hedging needs.\par     OCBC analysts said they expect Indonesia to remain a\par favoured recipient of net investor inflows in the Asia region,\par with the rupiah remaining a good "outperformer" candidate.\par \par     The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar at 0503 GMT.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen                    108.280     108.52        +0.22\par  Sing dlr                     1.356       1.3590        +0.20\par  Taiwan dlr      