\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  gain on stronger prospects for Fed rate cut\b0\par\par\uc2 677 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2019\par 06:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Indonesia rupiah gains as much as 1.05 pct\par     * Thai baht poised to strengthen for a sixth straight week\par     * Philippine inflation eases to 7-mth low\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Niyati Shetty\par     Jan 4 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gained against the dollar\par on Friday after dismal U.S. factory data spurred speculation\par that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  could switch from raising to cutting\par rates before the end of the year, and on signs of progress in\par Sino-U.S. trade talks. \par     Survey data on Thursday showed U.S. factory activity slowed\par more than expected in December, suffering the biggest drop since\par 2008 as the world's largest economy begins to lose steam.\par \par     Yields on two-year U.S. Treasuries sank below 2.4 percent,\par reaching parity with the Fed key rate. While, three- and\par five-year yields were even lower, an inversion that sometimes\par heralded recessions in the past.\par     Meanwhile, news that China and the United States would hold\par vice-ministerial level trade talks in Beijing next week further\par soothed risk-averse investors and boosted regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 OCBC Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a note to clients said that Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par may respond to the weaker broad dollar complex with foreign\par investor interest proving supportive for regional asset markets.\par     The Indian rupee was the second best performer in\par the region, strengthening 0.4 percent on Friday and was on track\par for marginal weekly gains. \par     Also gaining against the dollar was the South Korean won\par  and the Thai baht. The baht was in line to\par strengthen 1.5 percent this week, its sixth straight week of\par gains, however the won was poised to post a weekly drop of 0.7\par percent. \par     Elsewhere, gains in the Malaysian ringgit were capped\par after government data showed the country's trade surplus in\par November plunged as exports lagged behind imports.\par     The Philippine peso traded in a tight range as\par inflation in the archipelago cooled to a seven-month low in\par December, reinforcing expectations of a pause in interest rate\par tightening by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Chinese yuan, the Singapore dollar and\par the Taiwan dollar were marginally firmer. \par     \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH LEADS GAINS\par     The rupiah gained as much as 1.05 percent to 14,255\par on Friday, but had pared some gains by 0451 GMT. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par was on track to firm nearly 2 percent this week. \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  plans to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the domestic\par futures market to defend the rupiah, a official told Reuters\par earlier in the day.\par     This comes two days after Bank Indonesia's governor said he\par expects the rupiah's exchange rate to be more stable this year\par compared with 2018 as he is optimistic relations will improve\par between the United States and China.\par     \par    \par     The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar at 0451 GMT.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen               108.310     107.65        -0.61\par  Sing dlr                1.362       1.3636        +0.10\par  Taiwan dlr              30.873      30.886        +0.04\par  Korean won              1124.000    1127.7        +0.33\par  Baht                    32.060      32.16         +0.31\par  Peso                    52.610      52.58         -0.06\par  Rupiah                  14280.000   14405         +0.88\par  Rupee                   69.925      70.19         +0.38\par  Ringgit                 4.139       4.141         +0.05\par  Yuan                    6.863       6.8730        +0.14\par                                                    \par  Change so far in 2019                             \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 Latest bid  End 2018      Pct Move\par  Japan yen               108.310     109.56        +1.15\par  Sing dlr                1.362       1.3627        +0.03\par  Taiwan dlr              30.873      30.733        -0.45\par  Korean won              1124.000    1115.70       -0.74\par  Baht                    32.060      32.55         +1.53\par  Peso                    52.610      52.58         -0.06\par  Rupiah                  14280.000   14375         +0.67\par  Rupee                   69.925      69.77         -0.22\par  Ringgit                 4.139       4.1300        -0.22\par  Yuan                    6.863       6.8730        +0.14\par  \par \par  (Reporting by Niyati Shetty in Bengaluru; Editing by Simon\par Cameron-Moore)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-1-4T06:27:07.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190104ef1400fth\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
