\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Most Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  rise as dollar weakens ahead of jobs data\b0\par\par\uc2 711 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2018\par 07:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Patturaja  Murugaboopathy \par     Dec 7 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  clawed back some of their\par losses against the dollar on Friday after three straight days of\par decline, as lower bond yields and speculation that the pace of\par U.S. monetary tightening will slow next year softened the\par greenback.\par     The Indian rupee and the Indonesian rupiah\par led the regional gains, adding about half a percent against the\par dollar on Friday. Both \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were also supported by a\par decline in crude prices as India and Indonesia are major oil\par importing countries.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  is this month expected to raise interest\par rates for the fourth time in 2018, but investors have rapidly\par pared back their expectations for additional rate hikes next\par year. Investors now await November U.S. employment data due\par later on Friday for clues to how the world's top economy is\par faring.\par     However, despite the dollar's softness, analysts are still\par cautious on Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the short-term.\par     "In this midst of a more dovish Fed, AXJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should\par have more room for respite against the dollar," said Leong Sook\par Mei, ASEAN head of global markets research at \f28 \uc2 \f2 MUFG Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "But\par these gains are likely superficial at best in the short term\par given greater U.S. equity market volatility, \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yield\par curve inversion concerns, and higher oil prices."\par     The dollar index, which measures the greenback\par against a basket of six major peers, was little changed at\par 96.802. The index shed 0.3 percent during the previous session,\par closing at a one-week low and was down 0.9 percent from a\par 17-month peak hit on Nov. 12.\par     The South Korean won rose 0.3 percent after\par falling over 1 percent over the past two days, while the Thai\par baht also gained 0.2 percent on the day.\par     China's yuan firmed as market sentiment recovered\par from fears that the arrest of senior \f28 \uc2 \f2 Huawei\f28 \uc2 \f2  executive could\par spark a re-escalation in the U.S.-China trade war. \par     A recent Reuters poll showed China's yuan will breach the 7\par per dollar level within the next six months, and also predicted\par authorities would continue to exert control over the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par 2019.\par \par     \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par     The Indonesian rupiah rose 0.4 percent against the dollar on\par Friday, helped by a surge in local stock markets.\par     The rupiah has lost over 1 percent this week and was set for\par its biggest weekly decline in over two months.\par     Foreigners have sold about $76 million worth of Indonesian\par equities over the last two days, exchange data showed.\par     On Thursday, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par domestic non-deliverable forward (NDF) market to support the\par rupiah.\par     "(\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in NDF markets) will help delay, but not\par eliminate the demand for dollars,\u8221\'20\'1D said Frances Cheung, head of\par macro strategy at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Westpac\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par     The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar at 0555 GMT.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par    Change as of  0555                           \par           GMT                              \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest  Previous    Pct\par                             bid       day   Move\par   Japan yen             112.900    112.66  -0.21\par   Sing dlr              1.369      1.3692  +0.01\par   Taiwan dlr            30.829     30.857  +0.09\par   Korean won            1117.90    1120.3  +0.21\par                         0                  \par   Baht                  32.810      32.83  +0.06\par   Peso                  52.679      52.76  +0.15\par   Rupiah                14465.0     14515  +0.35\par                         00                 \par   Rupee                 70.588      70.90  +0.44\par   Ringgit               4.160       4.162  +0.05\par   Yuan                  6.877      6.8820  +0.08\par                                                 \par   Change so far in                              \par  2018                                      \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2               Latest   End 2017    Pct\par                         bid                 Move\par   Japan yen             112.900    112.67  -0.20\par   Sing dlr              1.369      1.3373  -2.32\par   Taiwan dlr            30.829     29.848  -3.18\par   Korean won            1117.90   1070.50  -4.24\par                         0                  \par   Baht                  32.810      32.58  -0.70\par   Peso                  52.679      49.93  -5.22\par   Rupiah                14465.0     13565  -6.22\par                         00                 \par   Rupee                 70.588