\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Most Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  drop on lower U.S. yields, growth worries\b0\par\par\uc2 746 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2018\par 08:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Patturaja  Murugaboopathy \par     Dec 6 (Reuters) - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were hit on Thursday\par as the U.S. bond market signalled trouble ahead for the world's\par biggest economy, while the arrest of a top executive of a\par Chinese tech firm in Canada for extradition to the United States\par shook risk markets.\par     An inversion of the U.S. yield curve, with the two-year\par yields moving above the five-year rates, has prompted recession\par worries and rattled global riskier assets. \par     There has also been a flattening of the curve further out,\par as spreads between two- and 10-year \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields\par tightened towards their narrowest in more than a decade on\par Thursday. \par     While few expect the U.S. economy to slow sharply anytime\par soon, an inverted yield curve has stoked fears of a recession\par down the road. Historically, the economy has taken anywhere\par between 12 months and 24 months to fall into a recession when\par the yield curve inverts.\par     Leong Sook Mei, ASEAN head of global markets research at\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 MUFG Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said the moves in U.S. bond yields will affect global\par equities and impact Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as well. \par     She noted that Asia is vulnerable to any U.S. slowdown as\par many of the economies rely heavily on the United States for\par trade. \par     "Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will definitely be affected, if the U.S.\par yield curve is inverted. It will come on top of the trade war\par concerns," said Mei.\par     Moreover, the arrest of a top executive of Chinese tech\par giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Huawei Technologies\f28 \uc2 \f2  fanned fears of a fresh flare-up in\par tensions between China and the United States.\par     The arrest comes at a particularly tricky time after U.S.\par President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  and his Chinese counterpart \f28 \uc2 \f2 Xi Jinping\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par reached a temporary truce in their trade war in a weekend\par meeting in Argentina.  \par     "Trump's threat that he is a "tariff man" should China\par refuse to comply with US trade demands, alongside the arrest of\par a high level \f28 \uc2 \f2 Huawei\f28 \uc2 \f2  executive, raises fear that the positivity\par from the Trump-Xi summit may unwind," said Wei Liang Chang, an\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     The Indonesian rupiah led the regional declines,\par shedding more than 1 percent, while the Indian rupee fell\par 0.7 percent. \par      \f28 \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept interest rates unchanged on\par Wednesday, as expected, on easing inflation worries and in\par efforts to persuade banks to lend more to support an economy\par that has lost some momentum.\par      The South Korean won, Thai baht,\par Malaysian ringgit and China's yuan, all shed\par more than a quarter percent each on Thursday.\par     \par     \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par     \par     The Indonesian rupiah dropped more than 1 percent\par against the dollar, hurt by a slump in its bond and equity\par markets. \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the domestic\par non-deliverable forward (NDF) market on the day,\par to support the rupiah, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's (BI) head of monetary\par management Nanang Hendarsah said.\par     Last week, its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it viewed the rupiah as\par still undervalued.\par     The rupiah has fallen 6.7 percent this year, and is the\par second worst performer in the region after the Indian rupee. \par     The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar at 0610 GMT.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par    Change as of  0610                           \par           GMT                              \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest  Previous    Pct\par                             bid       day   Move\par   Japan yen             112.790    113.19  +0.35\par   Sing dlr              1.370      1.3668  -0.26\par   Taiwan dlr            30.848     30.806  -0.14\par   Korean won            1118.60    1114.1  -0.40\par                         0                  \par   Baht                  32.820       32.7  -0.37\par   Peso                  52.690      52.74  +0.09\par   Rupiah                14548.0     14390  -1.09\par                         00                 \par   Rupee                 71.010      70.46  -0.77\par   Ringgit               4.165      4.1525  -0.30\par   Yuan                  6.877      6.8580  -0.27\par                                                 \par   Change so far in                              \par  2018                                      \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2               Latest   End 2017    Pct\par                         bid                 Move\par   Japan yen             112.790    112.67  -0.11\par   Sing dlr              1.370  