\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesia's  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves drop by $3.1 bln in Sept - c.bank\b0\par\par\uc2 426 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2018\par 13:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Rupiah down nearly 2 pct this week\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves level still above standard\par \par \uc2 * Reserves down $17.2 bln since end-Jan (Adds earlier governor, finmin comments, context)\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Oct 5 (Reuters) - Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves dropped by about $3.1 billion in September, partly due to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BI) \uc2 said on Friday, as the rupiah continued to trade near its weakest in over 20 years.\par \par \uc2 A broad retreat by investors from emerging markets, high oil prices and concerns over potential fallout from an escalating trade war between the United States and China all contributed to the pressure on the rupiah over recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost nearly 2 percent this week, and hit 15,190 to the dollar on Thursday, its lowest in more than 20 years, though it closed slightly stronger on Friday at 15,175.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's reserves stood at $114.8 billion at the end of September, equal to six-and-a-half months of imports, BI said in a statement, still far higher than the 3-month international adequacy standard, but representing a 13 percent decline from $132 billion in January.\par \par \uc2 The September reserves level "is able to support the external sector resilience and maintain macroeconomic and financial system stability", BI said.\par \par \uc2 Governor \uc2 Perry Warjiyo\uc2  earlier on Friday confirmed that BI has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah, though he stressed that BI was also also undertook smoothening \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  when trade became lumpy.\par \par \uc2 This week, the governor said local interest rates must be raised ahead of the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  to avoid "drastic" outflows, in a sign that BI may lift rates further before a widely expected Fed rate hike in December.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has increased interest rates five times since mid-May, by a total of 150 basis points, to maintain the attractiveness of Indonesian assets for foreign investors.\par \par \uc2 Separately on Friday, Finance Minister \uc2 Sri Mulyani Indrawati\uc2  said authorities were assessing global developments that triggered a rally in the dollar to determine whether they need to take further steps to halt outflows which have pummelled the rupiah.\par \par \uc2 The government has raised import tariffs, widened biodiesel use and delayed billions of dollars of infrastructure projects to cut import bills and reduce dollar demand onshore.\par \par \uc2 Indrawati said the government will support businesses to export more and may provide incentives. (Reporting by Nilufar Rizki, Gayatri Suroyo and Maikel Jefriando Editing by Clarence Fernandez & Simon Cameron-Moore) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-10-5T12:21:40.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020181005eea501okl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
