\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupee hits record low, \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  supports rupiah as oil prices weigh\b0\par\par\uc2 635 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2018\par 07:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * EM Asia trades flat on a dearth of cues\par     * Indian rupee breaches 73 to the dollar\par     * Further rupiah weakening spurs \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par \par  (Adds details on rupee, context, updates prices)\par     By Ambar Warrick\par     Oct 3 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee opened at a record low on\par Wednesday and  further weakening in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's embattled rupiah\par prompted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as an overnight spike in oil\par prices weighed heavily on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par    The rupee and the rupiah are highly exposed to fluctuations\par in oil prices, because Indonesia and India import most of their\par oil requirements.\par    Oil prices were steady after hitting a four-year high on\par Tuesday. \par     The rupiah's drop prompted the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, deputy governor Dody\par Budi Waluyo told Reuters. \par      The rupiah lost as much as 0.3 percent and stood at a more\par than 20-year low of 15,090.\par      The rupee shed as much as 0.6 percent to the dollar and hit\par a record low of 73.390. A plunge in the rupee had also spurred\par mild \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last month.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister said on Tuesday that the\par economy was adjusting "quite well" to higher U.S. interest rates\par and the fall of the rupiah, asserting that many of its economic\par indicators were good.\par     Most other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traded in a tight range on\par Wednesday in the absence of major cues.\par     Investors shied away from taking large positions ahead of\par crucial non-farm payroll data from the United States later this\par week, which is seen as foreshadowing the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \par policy tightening measures.\par     "There isn't really too much happening that's pushing\par volatility. There may be some concerns as to trade war impacts\par on Asia. We're still in a period of consolidation this week\par ahead of the non-farm payrolls," said Chang, Wei Liang, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par     The Singapore dollar inched lower against the dollar.\par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is a stalwart for investors in times of volatility,\par and as such has held most of its value, unlike some of its\par peers.\par     A Reuters poll of economists found that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Singapore\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is seen as likely to tighten policy again in\par October, albeit modestly, as policy makers worry about fallout\par from Sino-U.S. trade tensions. \par     Such a tightening is expected to benefit the Singapore\par dollar.\par     The Taiwan dollar was largely flat, while the Thai\par baht and the Philippine peso edged up. \par     Chinese markets have been closed all week for national\par holidays. South Korea's markets were also closed on Wednesday. \par     The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar at 0438 GMT:\par     \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR                              \par  Change on the day                                      \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen                    113.650     113.66        +0.01\par  Sing dlr                     1.374       1.3729        -0.07\par  Taiwan dlr                   30.667      30.668         0.00\par  Baht                         32.330      32.36         +0.09\par  Peso                         54.200      54.25         +0.09\par  Rupiah                       15070.000   15040         -0.20\par  Rupee                        73.360      72.91         -0.61\par  Ringgit                      4.137       4.14          +0.07\par                                                         \par  Change so far in 2018                                  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      Latest bid  End 2017      Pct Move\par  Japan yen                    113.650     112.67        -0.86\par  Sing dlr                     1.374       1.3373        -2.66\par  Taiwan dlr                   30.667      29.848        -2.67\par  Korean won                   1119.200    1070.50       -4.35\par  Baht                         32.330      32.58         +0.77\par  Peso                         54.200      49.93         -7.88\par  Rupiah                       15070.000   13565         -9.99\par  Rupee                        73.360      63.87         -12.94\par  Ringgit                      4.137       4.0440        -2.25\par  Yuan                         6.873       6.5069        -5.32\par  \par \par  (Reporting by Ambar Warrick in Bengaluru)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-10-3T06:38:55.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020181003eea300fl6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
