\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asian units fall on US tariffs, recover on hopes tensions can ease\b0\par\par\uc2 693 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2018\par 08:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds analyst comments, price moves and graphic)\par     By Patturaja  Murugaboopathy \par     Sept 18 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell\par early on Tuesday on news the United States was imposing more\par tariffs on imports from China, but some recovered as Beijing did\par not quickly announce retaliatory moves.\par     U.S. President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Monday that he will\par impose 10 percent U.S. tariffs on about $200 billion worth of\par Chinese imports and warned he would pursue more tariffs if China\par retaliates.\par     Up until now, the United States and China have applied\par tariffs to $50 billion of each other's goods.\par     As of 0600 GMT Tuesday, the Chinese government had not\par issued a statement on the U.S. move.\par     But on Tuesday morning, China released comments by Commerce\par Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Zhong Shan\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Monday to foreign investors that "there\par was no winner in a trade war and that cooperation was the only\par correct choice".\par     The comments provided some lift to China's yuan\par and other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The yuan, which fell as much as 0.35 percent early on\par Tuesday, trimmed its losses to just 0.1 percent.\par     Traders said the renewed Sino-U.S. trade tension piled\par pressure on the yuan, but market participants refrained from\par aggressively testing lows for fear the authorities may quickly\par step in. \par     The minister's remarks are "supporting Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 '\par sentiment on hopes that negotiations can proceed from here,"\par said Chang Wei Liang, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     The Thai baht, Singapore dollar and the\par South Korean won gained on the day, taking cues from\par the rebound in the yuan.\par      Thailand, Singapore and South Korea form a major part of\par China's supply chain and their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are the most affected\par if trade tensions escalate between the United States and China. \par     \par     The Indonesian rupiah led the regional decliners on\par the day, shedding more than 0.3 percent. \par     Saktiandi Supaat, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  research at Maybank, said the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the rupiah and bond markets and\par "increasing speculation that BI (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) could act again\par by hiking its policy rate through an out-of-cycle meeting"\par should help the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     A Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  deputy governor said on Tuesday the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market in a "measured manner" to\par maintain rupiah stability.\par     With a fall of 9.1 percent, the rupiah is the second biggest\par loser in Asia this year, after the Indian rupee\par     Declines in the crude oil prices propped up the Indian\par rupee. India is a major oil importer and lesser oil prices tend\par to reduce the external deficits, strengthening the rupee. \par     "Focus is less on the EM stress points and shifted towards\par the trade war so the rupee is likely to be less hurt vs. other\par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Maybank's Supaat.\par     The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar at 0540 GMT.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par     \par    Change as of  0540                           \par           GMT                              \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest  Previous    Pct\par                             bid       day   Move\par   Japan yen             111.950    111.83  -0.11\par   Sing dlr              1.371      1.3717  +0.05\par   Taiwan dlr            30.807     30.805  -0.01\par   Korean won            1125.90    1126.6  +0.06\par                         0                  \par   Baht                  32.580      32.63  +0.15\par   Peso                  54.140      54.11  -0.06\par   Rupiah                14925.0     14870  -0.37\par                         00                 \par   Rupee                 72.465      72.51  +0.06\par   Ringgit               4.144       4.137  -0.17\par   Yuan                  6.864      6.8553  -0.12\par                                                 \par   Change so far in                              \par  2018                                      \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2               Latest   End 2017    Pct\par                         bid                 Move\par   Japan yen             111.950    112.67  +0.64\par   Sing dlr              1.371      1.3373  -2.46\par   Taiwan dlr            30.807     29.848  -3.11\par   Korean won            1125.90   1070.50  -4.92\par                         0                  \par   Baht                  32.580      32.58  +0.00\par   Peso                  54.140      49.93  -7.78\par   Rupiah                14925.0   