\par\par \b \uc2 Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Has  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Market in 'Measured' Way: Director\b0\par\par\uc2 By I Made Sentana \par \uc2 199 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 2018\par 04:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA--\uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars in a "measured way" in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market early Monday even as sentiment on the rupiah improved from last week, a central banker said Monday.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  today must give a signal to the market when trading began (that \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  is in the market)," the nation \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's executive director of monetary management told The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Nanang Hendarsah said that there is sufficient dollar supply to meet demand. But \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more "decisively" if the dollar surges and prompts panic buying in the market.\par \par \uc2 The greenback was trading at 14,828 to the rupiah early Monday, slightly higher than its close Friday at IDR14,822.\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  was virtually the sole dollar supplier last week after the rupiah fell to its weakest level in 20 years due to worries about a spillover from the Turkish and Argentinian economic debacles and lingering trade tensions between the U.S. and China.\par \par \uc2 -- Write to I Made Sentana at i-made.sentana@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 10-09-18 0230GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020180910ee9a0002h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{