\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesia braces for prolonged pressure as rupiah slides\b0\par\par\uc2 574 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2018\par 13:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Rupiah hit 14,825/dollar, weakest since 1998\par \par \uc2 * President called a meeting for rupiah again\par \par \uc2 * BI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 , bond markets (Adds market movements, minister comments)\par \par \uc2 By Gayatri Suroyo and Kanupriya Kapoor\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Sept 3 (Reuters) - Indonesia is bracing for prolonged pressure on the rupiah amid souring emerging market sentiment exacerbated by Argentina's economic woes, the country's finance minister said on Monday, as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plumbed its weakest levels since 1998.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah hit 14,825 per dollar on Monday, the weakest since the Asian Financial Crisis two decades ago, before closing at 14,810. It has lost nearly 9 percent this year.\par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again on Monday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bond markets as foreign investors continued to sell Indonesian assets spurred by rising U.S. interest rates and fears of contagion from crises in Turkey and Argentina.\par \par \uc2 "We are monitoring global dynamics and need to be vigilant because the dynamics caused by the sentiment on Argentina is very high. The situation there is not yet finished, so we're anticipating these dynamics will continue," Sri Mulyani Indrawati told reporters after a meeting with President \uc2 Joko Widodo\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor.\par \par \uc2 Widodo had called a meeting with his economic ministers and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor to stress the importance of communicating to the people what was being done to stabilise the exchange rate, Coordinating Minister for Economic Affairs Darmin Nasution said.\par \par \uc2 "The president said 'don't let it be that you've done something, but the people said you have not'," Nasution said.\par \par \uc2 The government has forced a wider use of biodiesel starting Sept. 1 to reduce oil import bill. Officials have also announced plans to raise import tariffs on some consumer goods, though the list of affected items has not been made public yet.\par \par \uc2 Indrawati said authorities will monitor "in detail the behavior of market players" and take steps to prevent speculation.\par \par \uc2 BI has raised its benchmark interest rate four times since mid-May, by 125 basis points. It has also spent billions of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bond markets.\par \par \uc2 International credit rating agency \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2  has forecast Indonesia's policy interest rate could rise by 100 basis points through 2020.\par \par \uc2 Jahja Setiaatmadja, Bank Central Asia's chief executive, said he saw no sign of the sort of panic-selling seen during the crisis two decades ago, but added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could have to raise interest rates by at least 200 bps more by 2019.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's 10-year bond yield rose to 8.266 percent on Monday, the highest since November 2016, while the main stock index slipped 0.9 percent.\par \par \uc2 The cost of insuring exposure to Indonesia's sovereign debt hit an eight-week high, with the country's five-year credit default swaps jumping 5 basis points (bps) from Friday's close to 131 bps, according to data from \uc2 IHS Markit\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "With an external situation like the one we face now, we must assume that we need to continue to strengthen our fundamentals," Indrawati said.\par \par \uc2 "We are looking directly at our foundation and looking at where there are factors that are considered sources of weakness," she said. (Reporting by Gayatri Suroyo and Kanupriya Kapoor; Additional reporting by Maikel Jefriando; Writing by Ed Davies; Editing by Simon Cameron-Moore) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-9-3T12:03:47.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180903ee9301jv5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
