\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Lira falls as inflation spikes, rupiah hits 20-yr low\b0\par\par\uc2 1,045 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2018\par 11:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 3 (Reuters) - Turkey's lira led emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses on Monday after inflation spiked to almost 18 percent in August, while the Indonesian rupiah fell to its lowest level since the Asian financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 The lira was down 1.5 percent after Turkish consumer price inflation rose to a near 15-year high of 17.9 percent in August, up 2.3 percent month-on-month. Producer prices leapt 32.13 percent.\par \par \uc2 But \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments that the inflation outlook showed "significant risks" to price stability and that it would adjust its monetary stance at its upcoming meeting on Sept. 13 in line with this view helped contain the losses.\par \par \uc2 "The market is taking this as a signal for a rate hike at that meeting," said Inan Demir, senior emerging economist at \uc2 Nomura International\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "They should hike the one-week repo rate by about 500-550 basis points to address the deterioration in inflation \u8211\'20\'13 whether they will be able to do that is another question, but this is what is needed."\par \par \uc2 Turkey's Finance Minister Berat Albayrak told Reuters the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was independent of government and would take all the necessary steps. He also reiterated the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sell-off posed no risk to the country's banks.\par \par \uc2 Turkish five year credit default swaps fell 10 basis points (bps) from Friday's close to 569 bps, while Turkish stocks rose 1.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 This was despite the fact that Turkish manufacturing activity contracted for the fifth consecutive month in August as output and new orders slowed on the back of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis.\par \par \uc2 In another sign of the pressure on emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Indonesian rupiah fell 0.7 percent to its lowest level since the Asian financial crisis in 1997-1998.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah has weakened nearly 9 percent against the dollar so far this year, one of the worst affected \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the emerging markets sell-off, despite repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's inflation picked up in August, but remained within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target range.\par \par \uc2 Indonesian stocks fell 0.9 percent, while five-year credit default swaps rose to an eight-week high of 131 bps, according to \uc2 IHS Markit\uc2  data.\par \par \uc2 On a brighter note, Argentina's peso, which plummeted last week, firmed over 6 percent on Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctioned $250 million in dollar reserves and the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  issued a strong statement of support for President \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2 's government.\par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee also firmed 0.2 percent from last week's record lows after economic growth surged to 8.2 percent, its highest in more than two years. However, manufacturing growth unexpectedly slowed in August as domestic demand softened.\par \par \uc2 Weak factory activity data from across emerging markets helped push MSCI's benchmark emerging stocks index down 0.5 percent to one-week lows.\par \par \uc2 China's factory activity grew at the slowest pace in more than a year in August, reinforcing views of a cooling in the world's second largest economy as the trade dispute with the United States drags on.\par \par \uc2 The United States is still set to impose 25 percent tariffs on $200 billion of Chinese goods once a public comment period ends on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Chinese mainland shares fell 0.4 percent, despite the inclusion of another tranche of stocks in MSCI's EM index. Hong Kong shares slipped 0.6 percent weighed down by another 2.5 percent fall in Tencent amid China's crackdown on online gaming.\par \par \uc2 Other big fallers included South Korea, down 0.7 percent after factory activity contracted for a sixth successive month.\par \par \uc2 But Warsaw shares rose 1.05 percent, although Poland's manufacturing growth was at its lowest in 22 months. The zloty also firmed 0.2 percent against the euro.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's forint weakened a touch, with some disappointment that Fitch did not upgrade Hungary's sovereign rating in a review on Friday. For GRAPHIC on emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  performance 2018, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2e7eoml"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2e7eoml}}}\uc2  For GRAPHIC on MSCI emerging index performance 2018, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2dZbdP5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2dZbdP5}}}\par \par \uc2 For TOP NEWS across emerging markets\par \par \uc2 For CENTRAL EUROPE market report, see\par \par \uc2 For TURKISH market report, see\par \par \uc2 For RUSSIAN market report, see) Emerging Markets Prices from Reuters Equities Latest Net Chg % Chg % Chg\par \par \uc2 on year\par \par \uc2 Morgan Stanley Emrg Mkt Indx 1050.49 -5.47 -0.52 -9.32\par \par \uc2 Czech Rep 1075.41 +2.53 +0.24 -0.26\par \par \uc2 Poland 2360.81 +22.85 +0.98 -4.08\par \par \uc2 Hungary 37187.35 -46.05 -0.12 -5.56\par \par \uc2 Romania 8297.08 +22.54 +0.27 +7.01\par \par \uc2 Greece 722.49 -7.13 -0.98 -9.96\par \par \uc2 Russia 1087.08 -5.21 -0.48 -5.83\par \par \uc2 South Africa 52465.90 +1.89 +0.00 -0.13\par \par \uc2 Turkey 93901.73 +1178.34 +1.27 -18.5