\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Most Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  drift; rupiah at weakest since 1997-98 crisis levels\b0\par\par\uc2 752 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2018\par 08:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rushil Dutta\par     Sept 3 (Reuters) - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were flat in tight\par liquidity on Monday as escalating international trade tensions\par kept investors away from risky assets, while Indonesia's rupiah\par plumbed 20-year lows after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it was\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and bond markets. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's (BI) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is in response to an\par emerging market sell-off that has pushed the rupiah close to\par levels not seen since the Asian financial crisis.\par     The rupiah has weakened nearly 9 percent against the dollar\par so far this year, among the worst affected in the emerging\par market sell-off, which was exacerbated by a plummet in the\par Argentine peso and extreme volatility in the Turkish lira.\par     "\f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's (BI) commitment to maintain economic\par stability, especially the rupiah, is very firm. Therefore, we\par have stepped up the intensity of our \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," Governor\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Perry Warjiyo\f28 \uc2 \f2  told reporters on Friday.\par     The rupiah traded at 14,777 to the U.S. dollar at 0503 GMT,\par while 10-year bond yields rose to 8.220 percent.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Christopher Wong\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Maybank said the\par overall mood was cautious as emerging assets suffered in Turkey\par and Argentina, and as trade dispute grew.\par     Noting U.S. markets are closed for Labor Day on Monday, Wong\par said added that some traders were away and liquidity in local\par markets was thin. \par     U.S.-Canada trade talks ended on Friday with no deal to\par revamp the \f28 \uc2 \f2 North American Free Trade Agreement\f28 \uc2 \f2 , while U.S.\par President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  said last week he was ready to implement\par the new tariffs on China as soon as a public comment period on\par the plan ends on Thursday.\par     Meanwhile, the Malaysian ringgit hit its weakest since\par November even as an \f28 \uc2 \f2 IHS Markit\f28 \uc2 \f2  Purchasing Manager's Index (PMI)\par reading on Malaysia rose to 51.2 in August versus 49.7 in July,\par showing new orders expanded for the first time in seven months.\par \par     \par     \par     INDIAN RUPEE\par     \par     The Indian rupee rebounded from last week's record\par lows after data out late on Friday showed India's annual\par economic growth surged in the June quarter to 8.2 percent, its\par highest in more than two years. \par     Its local spot rate was 0.3 percent higher against the\par dollar at 70.785, after falling to an all-time low on Friday. \par     "Supported growth conditions provides room for the RBI\par (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) to defend core inflationary pressures\par and market volatility through further policy tightening. We\par retain our call for another hike in FY19," \f28 \uc2 \f2 DBS Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Radhika\par Rao\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a note.\par     DBS, however, doubted India could sustain a growth\par trajectory above 8 percent for the rest of fiscal 2019.\par     \par     ASIAN FACTORIES WILT IN TRADE WAR HEAT\par     \par     Surveys of purchasing managers released on Monday showed\par persistent pressure on key exporters China, Japan and South\par Korea. \par     China's vast manufacturing sector grew in August at its\par slowest in more than a year, while export orders also shrank in\par Japan and South Korea, pointing to increasing protectionism and\par concerns of reduced Chinese demand weighing on Asia's\par export-reliant economies.\par     The won was subdued as Korean stocks\par suffered, while the Chinese yuan was about 0.1\par percent weaker against the dollar.\par \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     \par  Change on the day at   0503 GMT                        \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen                    110.920     111.02        +0.09\par  Sing dlr                     1.370       1.3719        +0.12\par  Taiwan dlr                   30.707      30.731        +0.08\par  Korean won                   1113.000    1112.9        -0.01\par  Baht                         32.710      32.72         +0.03\par  Peso                         53.463      53.475        +0.02\par  Rupiah                       14777.000   14725         -0.35\par  Rupee                        70.785      70.99         +0.29\par  Ringgit                      4.122       4.108         -0.34\par  Yuan                         6.836       6.8310        -0.07\par                                                         \par  Change so far in 2018                                  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      Latest bid  End 2017      Pct Move\par  Japan yen                    110.920     112.67        +1.58\par  Sing dlr                     1.370       1.3373        -2.41\par  Taiwan dlr                   30.707      29.848        -2.80\par  Korean won   