\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Soften as dollar recovers, speech from Fed's Powell in focus\b0\par\par\uc2 781 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2018\par 09:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * EMFX Asia awaiting fresh cues from Fed Chair's speech\par     * China's yuan on track to snap 5 straight gaining sessions \par     * Sing. dlr posts biggest intraday fall in nearly 2 weeks\par \par  (Adds details on yuan, Sing. dlr, analyst comments)\par     By Ambar Warrick\par     Aug 23 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell against a resurgent\par dollar on Thursday as  investors awaited U.S. Federal Reserve\par Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jerome Powell\f28 \uc2 \f2 's speech on Friday for fresh cues. \par     Markets were looking to a speech by Fed Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jerome\par Powell\f28 \uc2 \f2  at the Jackson Hole meetings on Friday, amidst widespread\par speculation over a possible fourth U.S. rate hike this year.\par      A third interest rate hike for the year is widely expected\par from the Fed in September.\par     The U.S. dollar recovered after falling for six\par straight sessions, as the U.S. and China imposed 25 percent\par tariffs on about $16 billion worth of each other's goods. \par      U.S. and Chinese officials met on Wednesday to negotiate\par their trade ties, but there was little evidence that the\par low-level talks would result in immediate action.\par     "After the recent pullback in the U.S. dollar over the past\par few days we're just seeing some profit-taking and\par consolidation(in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 )," said Khoon Goh, ANZ's head\par of Asia research, based in Singapore.\par      "The Fed chair's speech (for the central bankers' annual\par meeting) at Jackson Hole at the end of the week is a big focus\par for markets, and I think right now we're at a bit of a\par consolidation phase at this point in time."\par      The Chinese yuan fell about 0.5 percent to the\par dollar, its biggest intraday drop in a week and breaking five\par straight sessions of gains. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has lost about 5 percent versus the dollar this\par year, primarily on fears arising from the U.S.-China trade\par dispute. \par     The United States is holding hearings this week on a\par proposed list of an additional $200 billion worth of Chinese\par imports to face duties.\par     ANZ's Goh said that the tariffs coming into play on Thursday\par  are largely priced in, but the planned additional tariffs could\par cause further volatility.\par     The Indian rupee softened versus the dollar as oil\par prices surged overnight after \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  data showed a\par larger-than-expected draw from crude inventories.\par     The rupee is the worst-performing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this year,\par having lost nearly 9 percent to the dollar in the year to date,\par reflecting in part India's exposure to oil price volatility. \par     Indonesia's rupiah shed about 0.4 percent due to\par high dollar demand from local importers, prompting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been struggling to stabilise the falling\par rupiah, and has hiked its benchmark interest rate four times\par since May. \par     \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par     The Singapore dollar shed as much as 0.37 percent to\par the dollar, its biggest intraday fall in nearly two weeks.\par     Singapore's inflation hit its fastest pace in nearly four\par years in July, bolstering the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's expectation of\par inflation coming in at the upper end of its 1-2 percent forecast\par range for the year.\par     "The Singapore dollar has strengthened to a key technical\par level and I think at this point in time there's a reluctance to\par push past a key technical level ahead of Powell's speech," ANZ's\par Goh added. \par     \par     The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar as at 0553 GMT.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     \par  Change on the day                                      \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen                    110.880     110.54        -0.31\par  Sing dlr                     1.371       1.3664        -0.30\par  Taiwan dlr                   30.772      30.730        -0.14\par  Korean won                   1121.800    1118.9        -0.26\par  Baht                         32.800      32.76         -0.12\par  Peso                         53.487      53.36         -0.24\par  Rupiah                       14633.000   14575         -0.40\par  Rupee                        70.090      69.81         -0.40\par  Ringgit                      4.103       4.096         -0.17\par  Yuan                         6.871       6.8388        -0.47\par                                                         \par  Change so far in 2018                                  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      Latest bid  End 2017      Pct Move\par  Japan yen                    110.880     112.67        +1.61\par  Sing dlr                     1.371       1.3373        -2.42\par  Taiwan dlr                   30.772      29.848        -3.00\par  Korean won           