\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesian rupiah does not reflect fundamentals,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  needed -c.bank deputy\b0\par\par\uc2 157 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2018\par 11:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Aug 16 (Reuters) - A deputy governor of \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday that its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is still needed to support the rupiah .               \par \par \uc2 "Rupiah now does not reflect fundamentals yet, thus we need \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since we need stability," Dody Budi Waluyo said.               \par \par \uc2 Worries about emerging markets and Indonesia's wider current account surplus recently have pushed the rupiah to its weakest levels since October 2015.               \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  rose its key interest rate 25 basis point to 5.50 percent. It has hiked the rate 125 basis points since mid-May.               \par \par \uc2 On Thursday afternoon, the rupiah was trading at 14,605 per dollar, a slip of 0.1 percent.               \par \par \uc2 Waluyo also said BI expects Indonesia's current account deficit to 2.5-3.0 percent of gross domestic product in 2019.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-8-16T10:13:46.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180816ee8g01bj5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
