\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  weaker, Indonesia's rupiah slumps to near 3-year lows\b0\par\par\uc2 693 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 2018\par 08:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Chandini Monnappa\par     Aug 15 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened against the\par dollar on Wednesday with Indonesia's rupiah touching a near\par three-year low and China's yuan hovering around 15-month lows as\par Turkey's shaky financial markets bruised investor appetite.\par     The Turkish lira, which plunged to record lows\par on Monday, has clawed back some of its losses but concerns that\par other emerging markets might face a similar fate continue to\par weigh on sentiment.\par     The U.S. dollar held firm near a 13-month high against a\par basket of major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on increased demand for safe-haven\par assets. The dollar index rose 0.1 percent to 96.793.\par \par     The Chinese yuan weakened as much as 0.37 percent\par to 6.908 as a slew of recent disappointing economic data hurt\par sentiment.\par     "I think the common denominator for fragile countries is not\par that they are emerging markets, but rather they have unresolved\par disputes with the U.S. president," said Taye Shim, head of\par research at Jakarta-based Mirae Asset Sekuritas.\par     "I think it's going to be very fragile going forwards and\par investors will need to recalibrate their investment agenda."\par     China's trade dispute with the United States is set to\par intensify next week with both sides planning to hike tariffs on\par more of each other's goods, threatening to pile more pressure on\par China's already slowing economy.\par     While U.S. tariffs have had little effect on China's trade\par and inflation so far, business surveys point to weakening export\par orders and there are concerns that a protracted trade war could\par lead to a sharper Chinese slowdown than expected a few months\par ago.\par     Prior to the market opening, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China\par (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 set the midpoint rate at 6.8856 per dollar,\par its weakest level since May 12, 2017, 161 pips or 0.23 percent\par weaker than the previous fix of 6.8695.\par     Singapore's dollar weakened 0.19 percent while the Thai baht\par  traded 0.3 percent weaker.\par     India and South Korean markets were closed on Wednesday for\par public holidays.\par          \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par     Indonesia's rupiah, which has been under pressure\par over escalating concerns about the economy's trade deficit,\par weakened as much as 0.49 to 14,646, as the country awaited the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rate decision.\par     Southeast Asia's largest economy posted a large trade\par deficit in July as imports surged more than expected, souring\par sentiment.\par      "It is naive to believe that Indonesia or emerging markets\par as a whole will see significant improvement in the trade balance\par from here," Shim added.\par     On Tuesday, Finance Minister Sri Mulyani said the government\par will impose a 7.5 percent import tax on about 500 goods that\par could be produced locally.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  is expected to keep its benchmark interest\par rate unchanged despite a plunge in the rupiah, a Reuters poll\par showed.\par     Additionally, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to defend\par the rupiah on Monday and again on Tuesday conducted auctions for\par cheaper \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap contracts to reduce hedging\par costs.\par    \par     The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar at 0555 GMT.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen                    111.280     111.14        -0.13\par  Sing dlr                     1.380       1.3777        -0.16\par  Taiwan dlr                   30.849      30.807        -0.14\par  Baht                         33.340      33.24         -0.30\par  Peso                         53.483      53.39         -0.17\par  Rupiah                       14625.000   14575         -0.34\par  Ringgit                      4.101       4.095         -0.15\par  Yuan                         6.906       6.8826        -0.34\par                                                         \par  Change so far in 2018                                  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      Latest bid  End 2017      Pct Move\par  Japan yen                    111.280     112.67        +1.25\par  Sing dlr                     1.380       1.3373        -3.09\par  Taiwan dlr                   30.849      29.848        -3.24\par  Baht                         33.340      32.58         -2.28\par  Peso                         53.483      49.93         -6.64\par  Rupiah                       14625.000   13565         -7.25\par  Ringgit                      4.101       4.0440        -1.39\par  Yuan                         6.906       6.5069        -5.78\par  \par  (Reporting by Chandini Monnappa in Bengaluru; Editing by Sam\par Holmes)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-8-15T07:26:45.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180815ee8f00tbl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*