\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Most Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  cautious; Indonesia's rupiah under pressure\b0\par\par\uc2 893 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 2018\par 08:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Chandini Monnappa\par     Aug 14 (Reuters) - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had some respite on\par Tuesday as Turkey's lira pulled back from Monday's record low\par and the U.S. dollar retreated, although Indonesia's rupiah\par weakened before the start  of a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy meeting.\par     The lira recovered after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Turkey's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par pledged to provide liquidity and cut reserve requirements for\par banks.\par     "With Turkey still not out of the woods despite some\par measures to address banking liquidity, we remain wary on EM\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for now as sentiment towards the EM complex will be\par hampered," Mizuho analysts said in a note.\par     The lira lost almost 10 percent on Monday and has shed more\par than two-fifths of its value so far in 2018 on concerns over its\par diplomatic rift with the United States and the risk of capital\par flight.\par     Tremors from the lira's plunge were also felt in South\par Africa and Argentina with the rand and Argentina's peso\par tumbling.\par     Argentina's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surprised by raising interest rates\par by 5 percentage points on Monday, but that was still not enough\par to stop the peso hitting a record low.\par     A ripple of selling was triggered on Friday when U.S.\par President Donald Trump announced higher duties on Turkish steel\par and aluminium exports, spiking EM \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility\par gauges.\par     Among safe haven assets, the dollar steadied at 110.85 yen\par , having hit a six-week trough around 110.11 on Monday.\par     The dollar was a shade softer against a basket of\par peers at 96.324, and gold prices slipped to their lowest in\par almost 20 months.\par     China's yuan strengthened 0.1 percent as the\par market shrugged off underwhelming macro-economic data.\par     Data out on Tuesday showed China's economy displaying\par further signs of cooling, with investment in the first seven\par months of the year slowing to a record low and retail sales\par softening. \par     Prior to Tuesday's market opening, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint\par rate to 6.8695 per dollar, its weakest level since\par May 26, 2017, and 66 pips softer than the previous fix of\par 6.8629.\par     The Indian rupee inched lower to 69.970, pulling\par back from record lows hit during the previous session. On Monday\par the rupee touched an all-time low of 69.62 per\par dollar.\par     "In our view, the rupee was overvalued. We had taken a view\par that the rupee would cross 70 versus the USD, and the fall in\par other EM \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has just exacerbated the fall," said\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dhananjay Sinha\f28 \uc2 \f2 , head of institutional research at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Emkay Global\par Financial Services\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Mumbai.\par     South Korea's won and the Singapore dollar\par strengthened 0.3 percent and 0.1 percent respectively.\par     The Thai baht and Philippines peso both\par weakened 0.2 percent. \par     \par   \par     Indonesian rupiah\par     \par     Indonesia's rupiah weakened 0.3 percent as the\par country grapples current account deficits.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the government have focused on\par relieving pressure on the rupiah, one of Asia's worst-performing\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this year.\par     "The rupiah remains a laggard on concerns that Indonesia's \par current account deficit may prove difficult to fund," said Wei\par Liang Chang, an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Joko Widodo\f28 \uc2 \f2  is set to hold a cabinet meeting on\par Tuesday to discuss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy a day after the\par rupiah weakened more than 1 percent.\par     "The Cabinet could consider new measures to encourage the\par repatriation of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earnings back into IDR (rupiah), or temper\par the current pace of imports to alleviate IDR pressures," said\par Mizuho's Wei Liang Chang.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to defend the rupiah on\par Monday and will begin its two-day policy meeting on\par Tuesday.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  has raised its main interest rate\par  by 100 basis points since mid-May to defend the\par rupiah but is expected to keep its benchmark interest rate\par unchanged on Wednesday, a Reuters poll showed.\par     The majority of analysts in the poll forecast BI would \par hold, but four who initially pencilled-in a hold changed their\par views to expect a 25-basis point hike after the rupiah slumped.\par \par     \par \par     The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar at 0542 GMT.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 