\par\par \b \uc2 After sprinting to aid rupiah, Indonesia c.bank could struggle in a marathon\b0\par\par\uc2 839 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 2018\par 08:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  c.bank most aggressive in Asia on rates, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Rupiah has lost more than 6 pct against the dollar this year.\par \par \uc2 * Level of reserves could become an issue longer-term\par \par \uc2 * BI, finance ministry looking at other ways to support \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 By Maikel Jefriando and Fransiska Nangoy\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, July 27 (Reuters) - \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  has done more than any Asian peer to defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid a global rout in emerging markets, but the fact that the rupiah has kept slipping suggests the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would struggle to maintain the pace in a prolonged battle.\par \par \uc2 Like many developing markets with current account or trade deficits, Southeast Asia's largest economy is hostage to forces outside its control, including rising U.S. interest rates, higher oil prices and the Washington-Beijing trade conflict.\par \par \uc2 And the difficult position Indonesia authorities face "may not end quickly", \uc2 PT Bank Central Asia\uc2  CEO \uc2 Jahja Setiaatmadja\uc2  told reporters on Thursday. "This is truly a marathon."\par \par \uc2 What differentiates Indonesia is how strongly the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has come out of the blocks.\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia (BI) \uc2 has lifted rates 100 basis points, twice what the Philippines has done, and has drawn more heavily on its foreign reserves than other Asian nations have.\par \par \uc2 Still, the rupiah is down more than 6 percent in 2018, nearly as much as the peso and Indian rupee. Bond yields went down after Indonesia's 50 bps June rate hike - which BI said reflected a "pre-emptive, front-loading and ahead-of-the-curve" policy - as investors gave their thumbs-up, but the reprieve proved temporary.\par \par \uc2 AN OPEN ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 For sure, economists do not perceive the lacklustre results in stabilising the market as a failure. Much is due to the fact Indonesia's economy is more open than India's or the Philippines' and its financial markets have larger foreign investor participation.\par \par \uc2 But limited results raise concerns about BI's firepower in case the Sino-U.S. trade conflict escalates and lasts for years, or U.S. heads into recession.\par \par \uc2 In such an environment, BI's traditional tools won't be enough. Further hiking rates at this pace will choke growth and add to pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are only $20 billion above the $100 billion mark at which some economists expect BI to turn less \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Given policy constraints, the economy "may not be able to able to handle more rate hikes", Paul Mackel, \uc2 HSBC\uc2  head of global emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  research in Hong Kong, said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Mackel said Indonesia might consider temporarily requiring exporters to sell some \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  proceeds and curb importers' \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases, similar to what Malaysia did in 2016.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joko Widodo\uc2  on Thursday pleaded with exporters to bring home earnings they currently keep offshore to help manage the rupiah from falling further, Finance Minister \uc2 Sri Mulyani Indrawati\uc2  said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Indonesian authorities, who know they need a multi-pronged approach, have revived an old tool and created a new one they hope will help the rupiah.\par \par \uc2 To give foreign investors more instrument choices, they auctioned 9- and 12-month Bank Indonesia Certificates (SBI) for the first time since 2016, raising 6 trillion rupiah ($412.51 million). The instruments, which foreigners can buy in secondary markets, help bring more capital in and let BI mop up the dollars investors sell to purchase the bonds and rebuild reserves.\par \par \uc2 Next week, BI launches a new benchmark for overnight interbank money markets, called Indonia, mirroring euro zone's and Britain's Eonia and Sonia. It aims to improve the transmission of BI rate moves to the financial sector.\par \par \uc2 Beyond reserves, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "has at its disposal a number of measures" to counter \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility, said Roland Mieth, emerging markets portfolio manager at PIMCO in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 FINDING DOLLARS\par \par \uc2 The finance ministry is also reducing rupiah bond issuance, hoping to meet some financing needs with additional foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans from lenders such as the \uc2 World Bank\uc2  and the \uc2 Asia Development Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We are getting many offers, but we are only taking what is needed to cover the shortfall in our rupiah bond issuance," Scenaider Siahaan, finance ministry director of borrowing strategy told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Foreigners, who hold more than one-third of Indonesia's government bonds, sold nearly 29 trillion rupiah ($2 billion) of local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds in April to June. Following BI's 50 bps benchmark hike, this month has seen 5 trillion rupiah returning.\par \par \uc2 While the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been "very much" proactive, that doesn't mean Indonesia is out of trouble, said Rohit Garg, emerging market fixed-income and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\uc2  in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 "If trade tensions do increase... there is only so much that BI can do to make sure that rupiah weakness is limited," he said.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Tabita Diela and Cynthia Silviana in Jakarta, and Marius Zaharia in Hong Kong; Editing by Marius Zaharia and Richard Borsuk) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-7-27T07:13:53.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180727ee7r008vu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
