\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Investors raise shorts on Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2 ; U.S. rate stance, trade war fears to blame\b0\par\par\uc2 1,003 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2018\par 08:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Bearish view on Chinese yuan at all-time high\par     * All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  see short positions being raised\par     * Indonesian rupiah bearish positions at highest since Oct.\par 2015\par \par     By Aaron Saldanha\par     July 26 (Reuters) - Investors raised bearish positions over\par the past two weeks on all emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , according\par to a Reuters poll, as U.S. rate hike concerns and a global trade\par war kept regional units under pressure.\par     Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have been hobbled in the past two weeks as\par the U.S. dollar firmed due to more clarity on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal\par Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's rate stance and as trade war ructions caused capital\par to depart from the region.    \par     The number of Americans filing for unemployment benefits\par dropped to a more than 48-1/2-year low for the week ended July\par 14 as the labor market strengthens further.\par     The lower unemployment figure, coupled with Federal Reserve\par Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jerome Powell\f28 \uc2 \f2 's upbeat comments on the U.S. economy in\par his latest congressional testimony, has lent credence to\par expectations of more interest rate hikes this year.\par     The dollar index touched its highest in over a year\par at 95.652 last Thursday before giving back some gains after U.S.\par President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  railed against the Fed's tightening\par policy.\par     In Asia, investors piled bearish bets on the Chinese yuan\par  to the highest on record, the Reuters poll of 11\par respondents showed.  \par     Over the last two weeks, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has weakened about\par 1.48 percent. Trump said last Friday he was ready to impose\par tariffs on all $500 billion worth of imported goods from China. \par     However, China said it has no intention to devalue the yuan\par to prop up exports.\par     Chinese state radio on Monday reported the country's cabinet\par signalling a shift to a more 'vigorous' fiscal policy featuring\par a corporate tax cut. \par     The policy shift is aimed at addressing potential trade\par shocks and liquidity concerns which have cropped up as the\par country looks to ease fears of a debt bubble.\par     Bearish positions on the Taiwan dollar rose the\par most, after those on the yuan. Taiwan's export-centric economy\par leaves it exposed to the potential fallout of a worsening global\par trade stand-off.\par     Indonesia's rupiah saw bearish positions being\par ramped up to their highest since October 2015, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par slid to its lowest in about 33 months earlier this week.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the country's bond and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets by\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has appeared insufficient to stem a\par more-or-less consistent weakening of the rupiah.\par     In the poll, the Thai baht saw short positions\par rising to their highest since mid-October 2016. The country's\par customs-cleared annual exports rose at a slower pace in June\par from the previous month, and less than forecast, commerce\par ministry data showed on Friday.\par     The Philippine peso has the second highest level of\par bearish bets in the region, the poll found.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 IMF\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Wednesday said it now expects the Philippines'\par current account deficit to rise to 1.5 percent of GDP by\par end-2018, compared with an earlier forecast of 0.3 percent,\par mainly due to increased imports of capital goods and raw\par materials.\par     Short positions on the Malaysian ringgit were at\par their highest in a month, with any hopes for a rate hike being\par dealt a blow as the annual inflation rate in June slowed to its\par lowest since February 2015, after the government abolished a\par goods and services tax.\par     Economists see \f28 \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  holding its key\par interest rate steady at 3.25 percent for the rest of the year,\par with the possibility of an easing if inflation slows further. \par     Short positions on the Indian rupee and Singapore\par dollar were also raised to the highest in a month. The\par Indian rupee touched an all-time low on Friday.         \par     The Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  positioning poll is focused on what\par analysts and fund managers believe are the current market\par positions in nine Asian emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : the Chinese\par yuan, South Korean won, Singapore dollar, Indonesian rupiah,\par Taiwan dollar, Indian rupee, Philippine peso, Malaysian ringgit\par and the Thai baht.\par     The poll uses estimates of net long or short positions on a\par scale of minus 3 to plus 3. A score of plus 3 indicates the\par market is significantly long U.S. dollars. The figures include\par positions held through non-deliverable forwards (NDFs).\par     The survey findings are provided below (positions\par in U.S. dollar versus each \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ):     \par     \par  DDMM  CNY    KRW    SGD    IDR   TWD    INR    MYR    PHP   THB\par  26/7  1.55   1.08   0.84   1.35  1.13   1.25   0.76   1.44  0.87\par  12/7  1.00   0.91   0.68   1.31  0.88   1.18   0.64   1.35  0.70\par  28/6  1.28   1.03   0.94   1.32  1.03   1.43   0.94   1.58  0.73\par  31/5  -0.15  -0.17  0.39   1.06  0.33   1.42   0.69   1.25  0.06\par  17/5  -0.28  -0.33  0.28   1.08  0.07   1.31   0.21   0.68  -0.14\par  3/5   -0.23  -0.38  -0.08  0.56  0.04   1.11   -0.24  0.47  -0.4\par  19/4  -0.52  -0.21  -0.44  0.14  -0.28  0.49   -0.19  0.74  -0.36\par  5/4   -0.65  -0.90  -0.50  0.10  -0.66  -0.05  -0.40  0.73  -0.60\par  22/3  -0.61  -0.48  -0.36  0.52  -0.59  0.41   -0.29  1.13  -0.72\par  8/3   -0.61  -0.64  -0.61  0.24  -0.54  0.19   -0.70  1.05  -0.99\par  22/2  -0.61  -0.32  -0.47  0.04  -0.92  0.04   -0.6   1.21  -1.02\par  \par  (Reporting by Aaron Saldanha, Additional reporting by Chandini\par Monnappa, Nikhil Nainan in Bengaluru; Editing by Sunil Nair)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-7-26T07:07:56.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180726ee7q007tn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
