\par\par \b \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Foreign-Exchange \highlight\uc2  Reserves Fall in May\b0\par\par\uc2 By I Made Sentana \par \uc2 141 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2018\par 12:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA--\uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to $122.9 billion at the end of May from $124.9 billion a month earlier, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday.\par \par \uc2 The decline was partly due to \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to defend the rupiah, which last month fell to its lowest level since October 2015.\par \par \uc2 Like many other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rupiah was under selling pressures due to the expectation of more aggressive rate increases this year by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  and trade spat between the U.S. and China.\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  last month raised interest rates a quarter percentage point twice.\par \par \uc2 Write to I Made Sentana at i-made.sentana@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 08, 2018 06:42 ET (10:42 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180608ee680018a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
