\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesia's new c.bank governor pledges focus on rupiah stability\b0\par\par\uc2 655 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2018\par 09:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to use policy rate, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help rupiah\par \par \uc2 * Rupiah strengthens slightly after Warjiyo statement\par \par \uc2 * Other tools would be used to support growth, he says (Adds details, context)\par \par \uc2 By Gayatri Suroyo and Maikel Jefriando\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, May 24 (Reuters) - Indonesia's newly sworn in \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor on Thursday promised to use interest rate policy to stabilise the rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term and to be "more pre-emptive" and ahead of the curve on monetary settings.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah has been among the worst performers among Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, losing more than 4 percent of its value, as investors slash their holdings in emerging markets in response to rising \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields.\par \par \uc2 "My priority in the short term is to strengthen steps required to immediately stabilise the rupiah exchange rate," Governor Perry Warjiyo told reporters at a news conference after his inauguration.\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Thursday, the rupiah hit its weakest level since October 2015 of 14,210 per dollar, before edging up to 14,160 after the statement by the new \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BI) \uc2 governor.\par \par \uc2 The main monetary policy rate and "dual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " of selling dollars and buying government bonds would be the main tools to shore up the rupiah, Warjiyo said. So far this year BI has bought 50 trillion rupiah ($3.54 billion) of government bonds from foreign sellers with most of the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  done in the past month, he said.\par \par \uc2 BI raised its key rate by 25 basis points to 4.50 percent last week, the first hike since November 2014.\par \par \uc2 When the rupiah extended falls the next day, outgoing governor \uc2 Agus Martowardojo\uc2 , said BI would be prepared to raise rates further.\par \par \uc2 Warjiyo reiterated his predecessor's view that the current weakness in the rupiah was due to external factors.\par \par \uc2 He said Southeast Asia's largest economy had sound fundamentals, predicting economic growth at 5.2 percent this year, with an inflation rate near the midpoint of BI's target range and a current account deficit under BI's healthy threshold.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hold a meeting with bankers and businesses, who use foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to convey BI's commitment to support the rupiah, Warjiyo said.\par \par \uc2 Such a meeting could prevent market from "overshooting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ", he said.\par \par \uc2 The new BI governor sought to draw a distinction between Indonesia and some other emerging markets, where there has been concern in the market about politicians meddling in policies.\par \par \uc2 While BI was working with the government and other regulators, President \uc2 Joko Widodo\uc2  had pledged to uphold BI's independence, he said.\par \par \uc2 Investors have sold the Turkish lira on concerns that its president would seek to influence monetary policy settings, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise interest rates by 300 basis points in an emergency move on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 In a bid to calm concerns about how policy makers can support economic growth, Warjiyo said BI would balance its monetary policy tightening with looser macroprudential rules and efforts to deepen financial markets and improve payment systems.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's GDP growth was 5.06 percent in the first quarter, below market expectations, and some analysts have said further tightening could choke economic activity.\par \par \uc2 "When we raise interest rates, it doesn't mean growth would slow immediately. The impact to growth will lag 1.5 years," Warjiyo said. "Meanwhile, the volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will probably only last a quarter."\par \par \uc2 Josua Pardede, an economist with Bank Permata in Jakarta, said he believes Warjiyo, who is an experienced central banker, "will be extra careful with the interest rate instrument" given the effects rate movements have on bank lending rates.\par \par \uc2 "If the pressure on the rupiah continues, there is a probability of another 25 basis points hike before the end of the year," Pardede said.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 14,140 rupiah) (Editing by Ed Davies and Sam Holmes) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-5-24T08:02:43.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180524ee5o00ais\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
