\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Malaysian ringgit dips in offshore trade on shock election result\b0\par\par\uc2 733 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2018\par 08:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Financial markets in Malaysia on holiday after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mahathir\par Mohamad\f28 \uc2 \f2 's win  \par     * Indonesian rupiah climbs in offshore trading after BI\par lends\par support\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Susan Mathew\par     May 10 (Reuters) - The Malaysian ringgit fell in\par offshore trading on Thursday on news of a shock election victory\par for opposition party leader \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mahathir Mohamad\f28 \uc2 \f2 .  \par    Mahathir's Pakatan Harapan Alliance scored a wholly\par unexpected win over Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Najib Razak\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Barisan\par Nasional, marking the first time a party other than the Barisan\par Nasional will rule since Malaysia gained independence from\par Britain in 1957.\par     The ringgit one-month and three-month non-deliverable\par forwards (NDF) weakened from Wednesday's close.\par \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bursa Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the national stock exchange, said trade\par would be suspended on Thursday and Friday in line with public\par holidays declared by the government.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said the holidays and suspension of trade was\par "buying time for Pakatan Harapan lawmakers to reassure investors\par that any change would be gradual and carefully managed". \par      A Bank Negara Malaysia spokesman said it would hold its\par policy meeting as scheduled later in the day. \par     "Malaysia is in unchartered territory as it has never had\par change of federal government before. The market had factored in\par a win for the ruling coalition so there will be some outflows on\par expectations of policy changes," said Jalil Rasheed, investment\par director at Invesco. \par     \par     RUPIAH \par     Indonesia's rupiah took the opposite tack in offshore\par trading on Thursday, with the three-month NDF strengthening to\par 14,385 from Wednesday's 14,411, after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it\par would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's financial markets were closed for a local\par holiday. The spot rupiah ended at 14,075 against the dollar on\par Wednesday, its third session of falls and hitting its lowest\par since Dec 2015.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia (BI) \f28 \uc2 \f2 had suggested it may raise interest\par rates as it said it was preparing to take monetary steps\par including adjusting the 7-day reverse repo rate - its key rate. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it would assess the level of inflation\par and the trade balance, as well as global capital flows and U.S.\par interest rates, before deciding whether to hike. \par     BI is to hold its monthly policy meeting next week. It has\par kept the interest rate constant since cutting it by\par 25 basis points in September last year. \par     \par     PHILIPPINE PESO, CHINESE YUAN\par     The peso rose 0.3 percent after news its economy\par grew 6.8 percent in the first quarter from a year earlier,\par matching expectations, driven by industry and services.\par     The data comes before the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monthly policy\par meeting later in the day when it is expected to hike the key\par interest rate as inflation picks up.\par \par     The Chinese yuan edged higher. China's producer\par inflation picked up for the first time in seven months in April,\par bolstered by surging commodity prices and suggesting its\par industrial demand remains resilient in the face of trade\par tensions with the United States.\par     Inflation in China is watched closely by analysts and\par investors for signs of a long-expected economic slowdown that\par would possibly tip a shift in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par  \par  Change on the day at 0440 GMT                     \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen               109.700     109.74        +0.04\par  Sing dlr                1.343       1.3459        +0.19\par  Taiwan dlr              29.919      29.928        +0.03\par  Korean won              1075.100    1080.9        +0.54\par  Baht                    32.120      32.08         -0.12\par  Peso                    51.813      51.991        +0.34\par  Rupee                   67.390      67.26         -0.19\par  Yuan                    6.365       6.3688        +0.05\par                                                    \par  Change so far in 2018                             \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 Latest bid  End 2017      Pct Move\par  Japan yen               109.700     112.67        +2.71\par  Sing dlr                1.343       1.3373        -0.45\par  Taiwan dlr              29.919      29.848        -0.24\par  Korean won              1075.100    1070.50       -0.43\par  Baht                    32.120      32.58         +1.43\par  Peso                    51.813      49.977        -3.54\par  Rupiah*                 14075.000   13565         -3.62\par  Rupee                   67.390      63.87         -5.22\par  Ringgit**               3.948       4.0440        +2.43\par  Yuan                    6.365       6.5069        +2