\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar's Comeback Knocks Stocks in Indonesia as Foreign Investors Flee\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ese Erheriene \par \uc2 594 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2018\par 14:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 One of the biggest casualties of the rising dollar is the emerging market of Indonesia, which is seeing heavy stocks selling by foreign investors.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the country's equities benchmark logged its third drop of at least 2.4% since the middle of last week.\par \par \uc2 The JSX Composite Index slumped 6.6% last week--the most of any major index globally, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2 , and its worst week since August 2013. Foreign investors pulled almost $400 million from equities. Sales in stocks of the country's biggest banks led the selling. The two largest both saw declines of nearly 15%.\par \par \uc2 Financials weren't alone. \uc2 Bumi Resources\uc2  , one of Indonesia's biggest coal miners, skidded 14% last week. But, highlighting recent volatility, the stock surged 16% Wednesday, and then fell 5% Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Selling has focused more on the market's most-liquid stocks rather than on sectors, said \uc2 Felix Lam\uc2 , a senior portfolio manager for APAC equities at \uc2 BNP Paribas Asset Management\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Indonesia has long been one of the most sensitive emerging markets to changing U.S. financial conditions given some 40% of the country's bonds are owned by foreign investors, noted Frank Benzimra, head of Asia equity strategy at \uc2 Soci\u233\'00\'E9t\u233\'00\'E9 G\u233\'00\'E9n\u233\'00\'E9rale\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Bonds fared poorly as the rupiah sold off in mid-April. The yield on Indonesian 10-year government debt climbed to 7.2% from about 6.6% in barely a week; it has since pulled back to 7%.\par \par \uc2 "The hunt for high yields makes the bond market attractive to foreign investors, but also makes it susceptible to periods of sharp outflows when financial conditions become less conducive," said Mr. Benzimra. "This, in turn, is reflected in movements in equities and \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Last month, the 10-year \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yield itself briefly topped 3% for the first time since January 2014. Worries about the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  accelerating the pace of interest-rate increases has also been causing jitters.\par \par \uc2 That helped weaken the rupiah as the dollar climbed to 2018 highs. On Wednesday, the dollar briefly topped 14,000 rupiah for the first time since January 2016.\par \par \uc2 Calling for calm, \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  staged a "sizable" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bond markets last week, saying it would remain in the market indefinitely.\par \par \uc2 The market tumult has raised the prospect of \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  boosting interest rates sooner than expected. It could encourage some capital to stay in the country. \uc2 DBS Bank\uc2  and ING predict a rise may come in the next several months when previous consensus forecasts were for no action this year.\par \par \uc2 The market worries come after the JSX index hit record highs in 2017, rising 20%. It climbed a further 3.9% in January, but has fallen 12% from its early-year peak.\par \par \uc2 In December, \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  raised its recommendation on Indonesian stocks to small overweight from underweight. But the investment bank admitted last week in a research note that the bullishness was "too early."\par \par \uc2 Still, most observers don't believe the recent declines are a harbinger of worse to come as investors largely remain bullish on the market.\par \par \uc2 Tuan Huynh at Deutsche Bank Wealth Management highlights the relatively young age of the country's populace and government reforms. While "investors hate uncertainty...medium to longer term I would still regard Indonesia's outlook as the best in this region."\par \par \uc2 Write to Ese Erheriene at ese.erheriene@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 03, 2018 08:49 ET (12:49 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180503ee530024f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
