\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  president pledges no gov't  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  in monetary policy amid weak rupiah\b0\par\par\uc2 157 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 2018\par 05:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, April 30 (Reuters) - Indonesia's President \uc2 Joko Widodo\uc2  promised on Monday that the government will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in monetary policy decisions by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in response to a weakening rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The government will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in monetary (policy) because it is the policy of \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 ," Widodo told reporters, adding that he believed the fundamentals of Southeast Asia's largest economy were "good".\par \par \uc2 BI Governor \uc2 Agus Martowardojo\uc2  last week said he would be prepared to raise the benchmark interest rate if the rupiah's weakness threatened the bank's inflation target or disrupted financial market stability.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah has been trading near its lowest since January 2016 in the past week. It traded at 13,870 a dollar at 0310 GMT Monday.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Maikel Jefriando; Writing by Gayatri Suroyo; Editing by Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-4-30T04:17:42.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180430ee4u004bo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
