\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Most Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  steady as dollar rally pauses ahead of \uc2 ECB\b0\par\par\uc2 763 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2018\par 08:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * S. Korean won best performer in region\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  meet in focus\par     * Malaysian ringgit, Taiwan dollar slip\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Chris Thomas\par     April 26 - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were steady\par against the dollar on Thursday as the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  paused from\par a rally driven by surging Treasury yields, while focus turned to\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy review later in the global\par day.\par     The dollar's index against a basket of six major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par was marginally lower at 91.142 at 0435 GMT, after having\par risen to a high of 91.261 on Wednesday.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (\f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) is set to keep policy\par unchanged on Thursday, playing down worries over recent softness\par in the euro zone economy and leaving the door open to ending its\par lavish bond purchase scheme by the close of the year.\par \par     "The U.S. dollar is breaking out and if the \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  is even\par slightly dovish tonight \u8211\'20\'13 or perhaps not hawkish \u8211\'20\'13 the euro\par could break wide open and with that, the big surge in the USD\par will have truly begun," Greg McKenna, chief market strategist at\par CFD and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  provider AxiTrader, said in a note.\par     The dollar hit multi-month highs against a basket of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recently, bolstered by higher \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields,\par led by the 10-year benchmark breaching the 3 percent threshold\par this week for the first time in four years.\par     In the region, the Indonesian rupiah struggled to\par recover from an over two-year low, edging up 0.1 percent in the\par afternoon session.\par     Indonesia is prone to capital outflows due to high foreign\par ownership of government bonds, and its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has tried to\par mitigate rupiah risk by buying sovereign bonds and selling\par foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . It has also urged businesses to hedge their\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  needs beyond minimum requirements.\par \par     Traders said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was seen buying rupiah in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around the 13,930 per\par dollar mark.\par      McKenna said the dollar appears to be set for another big\par rally, which could potentially push the rupiah through 14,000,\par and even beyond 14,200. However, "the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will\par certainly fight that," he said.\par     The rest of the regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  made small gains, with  \par India's rupee up 0.2 percent versus the dollar, the\par Singapore dollar 0.1 percent higher and the South Korean\par won rising as much as 0.3 percent.\par     Singapore's industrial production grew slightly more than\par expected in March from a year earlier as electronics output\par continued to show strong growth, data showed on Thursday.\par \par     On the losing ledger, Malaysia's ringgit slipped for\par a sixth straight session, shedding 0.2 percent to hit a\par five-week low.\par     The Taiwan dollar also fell 0.2 percent, touching\par its weakest level since early Jan.\par     \par     SOUTH KOREAN WON\par     \par     The won, which is closely tied to equity flows, recovered\par from three sessions of falls after tech giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung\par Electronics\f28 \uc2 \f2  posted a record quarterly profit and\par helped lift the KOSPI stock index more than 1 percent. \par     Earlier in the day, GDP data showed the country's economy\par bounced back last quarter, buoyed by booming exports of data\par memory chips and a boost from government spending, although\par private consumption was sluggish.\par     \par     The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar at 0531 GMT.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen                    109.300     109.41        +0.10\par  Sing dlr                     1.328       1.3282        +0.05\par  Taiwan dlr                   29.692      29.660        -0.11\par  Korean won                   1080.000    1080.6        +0.06\par  Baht                         31.590      31.58         -0.03\par  Peso                         52.247      52.22         -0.05\par  Rupiah                       13905.000   13918         +0.09\par  Rupee                        66.853      66.90         +0.07\par  Ringgit                      3.918       3.91          -0.20\par  Yuan                         6.324       6.3270        +0.04\par                               