\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  pressured as \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yield tops 3 pct\b0\par\par\uc2 779 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 April 2018\par 08:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Indian rupee at more than 1-yr low\par     * US yields hover above 3 pct mark\par     * China's yuan flat\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Chris Thomas\par     April 25 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remained\par under selling pressure on Wednesday as benchmark U.S. bond\par yields poked above the 3 percent level and lifted the dollar.\par     Indonesia's rupiah was left wallowing around recent two-year\par lows even as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stabilise the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The U.S. 10-year Treasury note's yield hit its\par highest level since early 2014, taking the dollar up 0.13\par percent to 90.881 against its index of six major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \par     "There\u8217\'20\'19s a lot more concern that it could spill over into\par regional bond outflows," said Chang Wei Liang, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     "If you look across the broader fundamentals, there is\par support for another uptick in yields with oil prices flirting\par with recent highs."\par     Higher oil prices point to increased inflationary pressure,\par which typically undercuts bond prices and supports bond yields.\par     Indonesia's rupiah was about 0.1 percent weaker.\par     High volatility in the rupiah led \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (BI) \f28 \uc2 \f2 to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , buying Indonesian sovereign bonds and selling foreign\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Agus Martowardojo\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Tuesday that BI would\par continue working to stabilise the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is also urging companies to hedge their\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  needs beyond the 25 percent minimum regulated\par requirement, in an attempt to temper dollar demand.\par     The Indian rupee was the worst performer in the\par region, falling as much as 0.5 percent to its weakest level in\par more than a year. \par     Indian shares were down 0.4 percent.\par     The Philippine peso, Malaysian ringgit and the\par Singapore dollar fell as much as 0.3 percent, while the\par Thai baht slipped 0.2 percent.\par     The Chinese yuan, which firmed slightly earlier\par in the session, was largely flat.\par     \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par     \par     The rupiah has fallen about 0.9 percent since the spike in\par U.S. yields last week, due to large foreign holdings of\par Indonesian bonds.\par     Foreigners held 39 percent of Indonesian government bonds at\par the end of March, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  data showed.\par     Due to a pick up in corporate USD demand and exacerbated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par market imbalance, "foreign reserves in April may drop by a\par larger magnitude than the $2 billion in March," Citi analysts\par said in a note.\par     "Yet, if the past is any guide, corporate demand for US$\par usually drops after the dividend season (May) and Eid\par festivities (mid-June) pass." \par     "Hence in the meantime, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  probably will refrain\par from any major policy shifts and may continue deploying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par reserves, which it has beefed up since 2016."\par         \par     SOUTH KOREAN WON\par     \par     The South Korean won shed 0.4 percent to touch\par its lowest in more than four weeks. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which is heavily influenced by equity flows,\par was also weighed by a drop in the KOSPI stock index,\par which was down for a fourth session.\par     "There\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of scope for surprise on the upside, partly\par because we\u8217\'20\'19re quite bullish on Korean Q1 GDP due later in the\par week," said Wei Liang.\par     South Korea's economy is expected to have returned to growth\par in the first quarter as exports of memory chips were strong\par enough to partly offset a steep decline in construction\par investment.\par     The advance GDP estimate is due 2300 GMT on April 25. \par     \par The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the\par dollar at 0529 GMT.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                    Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen                  109.060     108.81        -0.23\par  Sing dlr                   1.326       1.3220        -0.28\par  Taiwan dlr                 29.630      29.616        -0.05\par  Korean won                 1080.100    1076.8        -0.31\par  Baht                       31.480      31.43         -0.16\par  Peso                       52.320      52.191        -0.25\par  Rupiah                     13895.000   13885         -0.07\par  Rupee                      66.665      66.38         -0.44\par  Ringgit                    3.908       3.903         