\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Indonesia c.bank seen holding key rate in wake of Fed decision\b0\par\par\uc2 414 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2018\par 10:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/cb-polls?RIC=IDCBRR%3dECI poll data               \par \par \uc2 * 14 out of 15 analysts see BI keeping key rate unchanged               \par \par \uc2 * Rupiah this month hit its lowest in over two years               \par \par \uc2 * Decision due on Thurs, March 22, after 0700 GMT               \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, March 19 (Reuters) - \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , due to make a policy decision shortly after a \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  meeting that's expected to hike U.S. rates, will keep its benchmark rate unchanged on Thursday, a Reuters poll showed.               \par \par \uc2 Fourteen out of fifteen analysts in the poll expected \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 's (BI) 7-day reverse repurchase rate to be kept at 4.25 percent, where it has been since a 25 basis point cut in September.               \par \par \uc2 The other polled analyst predicted a 25 bp cut in the main policy rate.               \par \par \uc2 Some economists say BI will eventually have to follow the Fed and hike rates to support the rupiah, which this month fell to 13,800 to the dollar, its weakest level in more than two years. One analyst in the poll predicted a 25 bp increase by the end of June.               \par \par \uc2 But so far, inflation is in check, letting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hold the key rate as it tries to help boost sluggish lending and growth. Annual credit expansion was single-digit in 2017, while tepid consumption kept the GDP growth rising to well above 5 percent.               \par \par \uc2 BI cut the benchmark  by a total of 200 basis points in 2016 and 2017. The last time BI increased its key rate was November 2014.               \par \par \uc2 February's annual headline inflation rate was 3.18 percent, well within BI's target range. Price pressure is expected to remain modest as the government is seen maintaining domestic fuel prices, Gundy Cahyadi, an economist with DBS in Singapore said.               \par \par \uc2 In a March 15 note, Cahyadi said that while the rupiah's weakness is of concern, BI "is set to maintain its active presence in the market, but may delay any rate hike at this juncture."               \par \par \uc2 BI officials said the $3.9 billion drop in \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in February stemmed mainly from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prevent the rupiah from weakening too sharply.               \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week reiterated its view the rupiah is undervalued and said it will continue to be in the market to smooth out volatility.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-3-19T10:57:16.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180319ee3j00d7c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
