\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesia c.bank says rupiah should continue to strengthen\b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2018\par 07:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * BI sees rupiah strengthening to reflect fundamental value\par \par \uc2 * C.bank committed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in market to smooth volatility\par \par \uc2 * S&P: Firms might restructure debts if rupiah fell to 15,000 (Adds context, S&P comments)\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, March 14 (Reuters) - \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects the rupiah to continue to strengthen and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility to subside as markets price in anticipated hikes in U.S. interest rates by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 , a senior official said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 On March 1, after the rupiah hit a two-year low of 13,800 to the dollar, \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BI) \uc2 said it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. Since then, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has appreciated, and it was trading around 13,730 per dollar early on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Doddy Zulverdi, head of BI's monetary management department, said the current level "is not the (rupiah's) fundamental and it should be stronger than now".\par \par \uc2 Zulverdi, one of the candidates to become a member of BI's board of governors, reiterated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's commitment to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to reduce any volatility.\par \par \uc2 At its February policy meeting, BI said it anticipated four rate hikes by the Fed this year. On March 9, Governor \uc2 Agus Martowardojo\uc2  said the market is now more confident there would be only three hikes.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Martowardojo said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary stance remains neutral despite recent rupiah weakness. Its next policy decision is due on March 22, hours after the Fed concludes a meeting.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell $3.9 billion in February, mainly due to BI's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah and government debts in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . At the end of February, reserves stood at $128.1 billion, equivalent to 8.1 months of imports.\par \par \uc2 Zulverdi said rupiah weakness has had a limited impact on exports, but has likely had a bigger effect on delaying imports.\par \par \uc2 Xavier Jean, an analyst with Standard & Poor's Global Ratings, said on Tuesday a rupiah exchange rate of 15,000 a dollar is "the psychological level" at which even companies without cashflow problems would take the decision to enter into proactive restructuring with creditors.\par \par \uc2 "At 13,800, clearly debt is going up for companies that are not hedged, but we don't see that level today as a major problem because in 2015 they have been through that," Jean told reporters. (Reporting by Maikel Jefriando and Gayatri Suroyo; Editing by Richard Borsuk) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-3-14T07:12:44.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180314ee3e009fi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
