based \par                                          on traded USD/IDR spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign \par                                          exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions during \par                                          a specified time period which \par                                          are captured on a real time \par                                          basis, expressed as the amount \par                                          of IDR per one USD, for settlement \par                                          in two Fixing Business Days, \par                                          as published by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par                                          as the "Jakarta Interbank Spot \par                                          Dollar Rate USD - IDR", which \par                                          appears on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \par                                          website (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bi.go.id"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bi.go.id}}}\uc2 \f2 ), or as \par                                          published on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thomson Reuters\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par                                          Screen JISDOR Page (or any replacement \par                                          page or replacement service \par                                          as may be implemented for the \par                                          purposes of displaying the USD/IDR \par                                          weighted average spot rate), \par                                          or as otherwise made available \par                                          by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  (or its successor \par                                          as administrator), at approximately \par                                          10:00 a.m., Jakarta time, on \par                                          the Rate Fixing Date. Fallback \par                                          Provisions apply as set out \par                                          below. \par                                         The "Rate Fixing Date" means \par                                          the date that is five (5) Fixing \par                                          Business Days prior to the applicable \par                                          Fixed Rate Interest Payment \par                                          Date or Maturity Date, as the \par                                          case may be. The Rate Fixing \par                                          Date shall be subject to adjustment \par                                          as follows: if the scheduled \par                                          date of the Rate Fixing Date \par                                          is not a Relevant Business Day, \par                                          then the Rate Fixing Date will \par                                          be the first preceding day that \par                                          is a Relevant Business Day. \par                                          "Fixing Business Day" means \par                                          a day (other than a Saturday \par                                          or a Sunday) on which banks \par                                          and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets \par                                          are open for business in Jakarta. \par                                         "Fallback Provisions": Should \par                                          no USD/IDR weighted average \par                                          spot rate appear on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \par                                          website (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bi.go.id"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bi.go.id}}}\uc2 \f2 ) as the \par                                          "Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar \par                                          Rate USD - IDR", or on Thomson \par                                          Reuters Screen JISDOR Page (or \par                                          on such replacement page or \par                                          replacement service as described \par                                          above), or be otherwise made \par                                          available by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par                                          (or its successor as administrator), \par                                          on the Rate Fixing Date, then \par                                          the IDR Rate for such Rate Fixing \par                                          Date shall be determined by \par                                          the Calculation Agent by requesting \par                                          quotations for the mid USD/IDR \par                                          spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate from \par                                          five banks active in the USD/IDR \par                                          \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par                                          markets as selected by the Calculation \par                                          Agent (such banks, the "Reference \par                                          Banks") either (i) at or about \par                                          10:00 a.m. Jakarta time on the \par                                          first day (other than a Saturday \par                                          or a Sunday) following the Rate \par                                          Fixing Date, if such day is \par                                          a Relevant Business Day or (ii) \par                                          at or about 10:00 a.m. Jakarta \par                                          time on the Rate Fixing Date, \par                                          if the first day (other than \par                                          a Saturday or a Sunday) following \par                                          the Rate Fixing Date is not \par                                          a Relevant Business Day. \par                                         If five or four quotations are \par                                          provided by Reference Banks \par                                          as requested, the IDR Rate shall \par                                          be the arithmetic mean (rounded \par                                          to the nearest whole IDR, with \par                                          IDR 0.5 being rounded upwards) \par                                          of the remaining three or two \par                                          such quotations (expressed as \par                                          the number of IDR per one USD), \par                                          as the case may be, after disregarding \par                                          the highest quotation and the \par                                          lowest quotation; provided, \par                                          that if two or more such quotations \par                                          are the highest such quotations, \par                                          then only one of such quotations \par                                          shall be disregarded; and provided \par                                          further, that if two or more \par                                          such quotations are the lowest \par                                          such quotations, then only one \par                                          of such lowest quotations shall \par                                          be disregarded. \par                                          If only three or two quotations \par                                          are provided as requested, the \par                                          IDR Rate shall be the arithmetic \par                                          mean (rounded to the nearest \par                                          whole IDR, with IDR 0.5 being \par                                          rounded upwards) of such quotations \par                                          (expressed as the number of \par                                          IDR per one USD). \par                                          If only one or no quotations \par                                          are provided as requested, or \par                                          if the Calculation Agent determines \par                                          in its sole discretion that \par                                          no suitable Reference Banks \par                                          active in the USD/IDR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par                                          or \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets \par                                          will provide quotations, the \par                                          Calculation Agent shall be entitled \par                                          to calculate the IDR Rate acting \par                                          in good faith in a commercially \par                                          reasonable manner, having taken \par                                          into account relevant market \par                                          practice, by reference to such \par                                         